# Guided L1: a named relationship with `example` bindings. This is the
# first-ten-minutes shape (emath-v9-06-2rdq.18): emath expands it, prints
# what it inferred, and never picks a hidden default.
#
#   emath expand    language/examples/intro/l1_guided.emath   -> the desugared function
#   emath exactness language/examples/intro/l1_guided.emath   -> what emath inferred
#
# A dimension raise on the printed budget is propose-only: the file on
# disk is never rewritten. After `emath freeze --out <frozen>` the same
# raise refuses E-SYN-155 — frozen sources do not raise.
slope = 2 * x + b
example x = 3
example b = 1
